Subject: [PATCH] vayu_wifi W25n: the HTT TX slot was freed before its busy bit was set (pool leaked
 all 64 slots after ~90 frames); kernel DHCP off by default; addresses kept in wire order

Base: /mnt/ramdisk/ds-wifi2 as run 143839 (kernel mach-wifi25m).  WPA2 completes and the link
holds; iOS configd itself gets 10.1.30.41 over DHCP, then TX dies: "frames tx 92 ... 52/285/371
dropped" while rx keeps growing, and the counters read "94 sent, 94 completed by the firmware;
status 0:89 1:3 2:2".

The bug: vayu_scan_tx_frame() set the slot's bit in tx_busy only AFTER tx_ops->htt_send()
returned.  tx_frame() runs on the interface's thread; the completions are processed by the poll
thread, and htt_send waits for the CE doorbell (the log's "done after 1 ms").  A completion could
therefore be processed for a frame whose bit was not up yet: the handler cleared nothing, the
sender then set the bit, and the slot stayed busy for good.  Roughly one slot leaked per burst
until all 64 were gone -- after 92 frames every new frame found id == TX_SLOTS and was dropped in
our code (net.tx_drop), which is exactly the 52 -> 285 -> 371 growth while tx stayed at 92.

Changes:
 - bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_scan.c: the busy bit goes up before the send (and comes off again if the send
   fails); the completion handler and the allocator both take tx_lock, so a free cannot be lost
   between them.  Drops are counted by reason (no slot, send, length, pool).
 - a line every 10 s (bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_sta.c, keep mode): sent, completed, the completion status
   histogram, slots in flight / free of 64, the four drop counters, and the WMI endpoint's HTC
   credits (vayu_htcc_credits(); the HTT endpoint has no credit flow).
 - bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_net.c: the kernel DHCP client is off unless vayu_wifi_dhcp=1 (iOS configd is
   the one that should hold the lease; ours raced it and NAKed).  When it is on, addresses are
   kept as the four bytes of the packet: option 50 was built from a host-order u32, so the
   REQUEST asked for 41.30.1.10 instead of 10.1.30.41 and the server NAKed; the offer/bound lines
   printed the same way.  Options 50/54, ARP and ICMP now use the bytes as received.
 - job 1011 no longer passes vayu_wifi_dhcp=1.

Expected on the next run: no growth of "drops: no slot" after the first bursts, "slots in flight"
staying small (single digits), tx climbing with iOS traffic, and no "nak from the server" (our
client stays off; configd keeps its lease).

